# Make sentinel directory — tracks completed build/init/bootstrap steps.
# Delete individual sentinels to force steps to rerun; delete the whole
# directory to force a full rebuild:
#   rm .make/bootstrap && make bootstrap   # re-run bootstrap only
#   rm -rf .make       && make             # full rebuild
.make/

# Testbed runtime data and secrets — never commit these.
# They are generated by  ./testbed.sh init  into $TESTBED_ROOT (default: ~/cvmfs-testbed).
# If TESTBED_ROOT is inside this repo tree, keep it out of git:
cvmfs-testbed/
*.env
# *.env does NOT match .env.s3 (it ends in .s3), and that file holds the MinIO
# password. The .example template stays tracked.
.env.s3

# Editor / OS artefacts
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
data/payload/
repo-seed.tar.gz
/data/
/repos/
# Generated runtime config: signing keys, gateway secrets, the S3 config
# (which carries the MinIO access/secret key), and cvmfs-prepub/config.yaml
# (generated by init.sh from its heredoc — the heredoc is the source of
# truth, so no sample copy is tracked).  Defensive only — these normally
# live in $TESTBED_ROOT (default ~/cvmfs-testbed), which is NOT this checkout
# unless the two happen to coincide.
/config/*
/software/
/scripts/software/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/scripts/testbed-console-cert.pem
/scripts/testbed-console-key.pem
